.el .ds Aq '
.TH taurctl-upgrade 1  "taurctl-upgrade " 
.SH NAME
taurctl\-upgrade \- Upgrade the installed TAUR package from a GitHub Release
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtaurctl upgrade\fR [\fB\-\-server\fR] [\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fB\-\-config\-dir\fR] [\fB\-\-restart\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-health\-url\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-password\-stdin\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Upgrade the installed TAUR package from a GitHub Release.
.PP
Downloads the native package for this machine (Debian/Ubuntu, Fedora/RHEL, or Arch; Linux x86_64 only), verifies SHA256SUMS, and installs it with apt\-get, dnf, or pacman. Configuration, the database, and git repositories are left in place. A package rollback cannot undo a database schema migration. The service is not restarted unless `\-\-restart` is given.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-server\fR \fI<SERVER>\fR
Server URL (overrides TAUR_SERVER and the config file)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTAUR_SERVER\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR \fI<VERSION>\fR
Release tag or version (for example 1.5.0 or v1.5.0). Default: the latest GitHub Release
.TP
\fB\-\-config\-dir\fR \fI<CONFIG_DIR>\fR
Config directory (default: $TAURCTL_CONFIG_DIR, else $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/taurctl)
.TP
\fB\-\-restart\fR
Restart the taur service after installing and check GET /api/v1/server. If the check fails, the previous package is reinstalled when it was retained
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the planned package and commands without downloading or installing
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print raw JSON
.TP
\fB\-\-health\-url\fR \fI<URL>\fR
URL used for the post\-restart health check (default: http://127.0.0.1:<TAUR_BIND port>)
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Don\*(Aqt ask for confirmation
.TP
\fB\-\-password\-stdin\fR
Read the password from the first line of stdin instead of prompting
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  taurctl upgrade
  taurctl upgrade \-\-version 1.5.0
  taurctl upgrade \-\-version 1.5.0 \-\-restart \-y
